From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brian McKenna <brian@brianmckenna.org>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 06:43:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 17/17] fix(shader): name the address an SRT walk could not
 read through user data

A descriptor read through a user-data pointer to memory the request does
not hold is refused at record time ("descriptor source N dword 0:
ReadConst(GetSrtResource, ...) where slot M = LoadAddressU32(
GetAddressResource(GetUserData, ...))"), but the error did not say which
pointer or address: a host that left a region out of the request (a
title's mesh stages read their tables through user SGPRs into GPU memory
a host had not listed) could not tell which.

The refusal now ends with "it reads 0x... through user data word N,
which the request's memory does not hold" (or "through a computed
pointer"). Nothing else changes: such a read is still refused.

Tested: tests/DescriptorSelectionTests.cpp loads a V# through a
user-data pointer to unmapped memory and checks the message names the
word and the address; without the change it names neither.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
